  "behavior": [
    "Exact named/transparent {i64,i64} objects reuse the existing 16-byte integer frame storage.",
    "Exact {i64,i16,[6xi8]} and {{i64,i64},i16,[6xi8]} wrappers use existing 16/24-byte array frame storage in a private codegen view.",
    "Native layout, complete type shape, unique named definitions, alignment and single-object counts are checked before conversion. Source records and nested call arguments remain unchanged.",
    "Typed byte-address admission checks the current 16/24-byte storage extent before emitting; invalid offsets publish no instructions or binding.",
    "Mixed pair/wrapper copies recognize the bounded literal integer extension produced by the earlier private conversion.",
    "Four permanent native functions check copies, all defined padding bytes, narrow tags, helper calls, live values, alignment and guards across direct/release routes in three modes."
  ],
  "known_boundaries": [
    "Packed, floating/vector, unresolved, cyclic and duplicate named shapes; dynamic/multiple objects and excessive alignment; incompatible target layouts.",
    "Aggregate value/call/return ABI forms beyond existing support, nondefault address spaces, unsupported barriers and dynamic/oversized wrapper copies.",
    "Fibonacci 56-byte array stride, narrower call ABI forms and remaining whole-program boundaries."
  ],
